USE NS re DB kb;
UPSERT source:gsta_effect_decode_model_measured SET kind='measurement',
  ref='tools/render-replica-poc/_live_fx2.gsta.mcrr + _live_fx2.mirror.zcst; _efxprobe2.mjs / _wrapchk.mjs / _scan_fx.mjs / _efxpool.mjs; marvelous2 bank12 loc_8C1244B0 + gen_submit_params.c read_template',
  note='Effect-Poly decode MEASURED 2026-06-21. (1) Per-part submit loc_8C1244B0 reads PCW/ISP/TSP/TCW from the RESIDENT rectab template *(0x8C2DAD4c)+idxtab[*r13]*0x20 (gen_submit_params.c read_template) NOT from GFX1/GFX2 -> the TCW already carries the texture VRAM addr; effects are never per-frame LZSS-decoded. (2) Effect-Poly bank is an absolute-pointer directory: head 0x0CED0010, base *(0x0CED0008)=0x0CED03D8, 0x10B entries {e0=w|(h<<16), e4=PVR PixelFmt|0x300 (mask &0xFFFF not &0xFF; e4&7=fmt 0=ARGB1555 1=RGB565 2=ARGB4444), e8=texel ptr, ec=0}, 25 valid [0..24] terminated by e0==0. (3) e8 (0x0CDA4000=13.6MB) is a SYSTEM-RAM source of already-PVR twiddled 16-bit texels (RAM-nz 25947/32768), NOT a VRAM addr (>8MB DC VRAM). The engine DMAs to a dynamically-allocated VRAM slot; dir[0] exact texels found resident in captured VRAM at 0x4BF000 (content match), NOT at e8 nor e8&vram_mask(0x5A4000=different data). (4) That VRAM ships verbatim in the GSTA prefix so a real effect quad samples the resident slot via its template TCW -> NO client decode needed. The only bug was old code corrupting VRAM by mis-LZSS-parsing the directory (pink/blue garble); the fc7072a69 SKIP removes exactly that and is PROVEN correct. (5) _live_fx2 has effect TEXTURES resident but ZERO active effect render nodes (objpool 1199 frames) and ZERO engine additive sprites (_scan_fx DstInstr==ONE never appears) -> no effect was on-screen; live binding + GAP2 per-cell TSP still need a contact frame.';

UPSERT finding:gsta_effect_decode_skip_proven SET
  statement='GSTA effect rendering GAP 1 (decode) SETTLED 2026-06-21 by measurement: the faithful client action is the SKIP (commit fc7072a69), now PROVEN correct, not a placeholder. The engine submit (bank12 loc_8C1244B0) reads the per-part TCW from the resident rectab template, and an effect texture is already resident in the shipped GSTA-prefix VRAM at an engine-allocated slot (dir[0] texels measured at VRAM 0x4BF000), so a real effect quad samples correct texels with no client decode. The Effect-Poly directory e8 pointers (0x0CDA4000=13.6MB) are SYSTEM-RAM sources, NOT VRAM dests; an attempted directory->VRAM upload (copy e8 texels to e8&mask) was WRONG (different VRAM address, different data) and was reverted after measurement. gstaDecodeBodies keeps continue for gfx1 in [0x0CED0000,0x0CEE0000) with the corrected in-code rationale. CLIENT REBUILT (build/flycast.exe). OPEN: the offline capture _live_fx2 has effect textures resident but no live effect render node and no engine additive sprite across 1199 frames, so the live node->VRAM-slot binding and GAP 2 (per-cell TSP additive vs the gfx1-bank heuristic, engine type==4 finalize loc_8c124740) still need a contact-frame capture to A/B. Best ground-truth tool here = marvelous2 + the offline RAM capture (byte-level residency), NOT Oracle/ASMTRACE (headless never put an effect on screen) and NOT a wire diff (shows nothing when no effect renders). Branch feat/render-replica-live.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-21';

RELATE finding:gsta_effect_decode_skip_proven->cites->source:gsta_effect_decode_model_measured;
RELATE finding:gsta_effect_decode_skip_proven->cites->routine:loc_8c0344d4;
RELATE finding:gsta_effect_decode_skip_proven->about->finding:objs_effect_blend_gap;
